{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "canvas-30-agent-layout-50-tool-surface-00-overview",
  "title": "The gesture tool surface",
  "root": "b-ts-ov-root",
  "blocks": {
    "b-ts-ov-root": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-root",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {
        "covers": "Why the layout agent's tools are factored by editing gesture rather than by CRUD per kind, the full thirty-two-tool roster in its registration order, the calls the surface absorbs rather than adds, the scope it deliberately excludes, and a map of the rest of this tier.",
        "format": "mdx",
        "type": "overview",
        "concepts": [
          "gesture factoring",
          "tool roster",
          "capability matrix",
          "structural parameters",
          "surface scope"
        ]
      },
      "children": [
        "b-ts-ov-title-1",
        "b-ts-ov-lede-2",
        "b-ts-ov-consequence-matrix-3",
        "b-ts-ov-consequence-structural-4",
        "b-ts-ov-trace-5",
        "b-ts-ov-roster-heading-6",
        "b-ts-ov-roster-source-7",
        "b-ts-ov-roster-table-8",
        "b-ts-ov-absorbed-heading-9",
        "b-ts-ov-absorbed-lede-10",
        "b-ts-ov-absorbed-measure-11",
        "b-ts-ov-absorbed-distribute-12",
        "b-ts-ov-absorbed-route-13",
        "b-ts-ov-scope-heading-14",
        "b-ts-ov-scope-lede-15",
        "b-ts-ov-scope-multi-16",
        "b-ts-ov-scope-extend-17",
        "b-ts-ov-scope-annotation-18",
        "b-ts-ov-scope-close-19",
        "b-ts-ov-tier-heading-20",
        "b-ts-ov-tier-lede-21",
        "b-ts-ov-tier-gestures-22",
        "b-ts-ov-tier-grid-23",
        "b-ts-ov-tier-pipeline-24",
        "b-ts-ov-tier-registration-25"
      ]
    },
    "b-ts-ov-title-1": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-title-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 1
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The gesture tool surface"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-lede-2": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-lede-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The agent's complete tool surface — every board-mutating gesture plus the perception, annotation, and run-lifecycle calls — is factored by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "editing gesture",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " rather than by CRUD per kind. Each tool is one thing a person does in one motion on the real canvas: place a thing, move it, resize it, retitle it, slide a connector segment out of the way. Two consequences fall out of that framing."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-consequence-matrix-3": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-consequence-matrix-3",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The tool list is the capability matrix.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " \"Can a section's border change?\" is answered by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "change_section_border",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " existing and its schema naming its target kind — not by prose inside a catch-all patch."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-consequence-structural-4": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-consequence-structural-4",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Required parameters are structural.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " Every verb's schema states exactly what that gesture needs. There are no everything-optional patches."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-trace-5": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-trace-5",
      "type": "observation",
      "props": {
        "title": "A trace reads like an editing session"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A run's tool calls read as "
        },
        {
          "insert": "place, place, connect, move_by, resize, change_color",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — the sequence a person would perform, in the order they would perform it. That is what the playback rail animates and what the eval judges read."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-roster-heading-6": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-roster-heading-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The roster"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-roster-source-7": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-roster-source-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The surface is thirty-two tools: twenty-five board-mutating gestures in six groups, listed by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "operationTools",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools/operations/index.ts",
              "symbol": "operationTools"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", plus seven workflow calls listed by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "workflowTools",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/src/service/session/tools/workflow/index.ts",
              "symbol": "workflowTools"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Those two arrays are the single source the agent catalog registers from and the "
        },
        {
          "insert": "<capabilities>",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " block derives from, so a tool defined in a group module is not on the surface until it is listed there. The table below is their registration order, which is roughly the order a board gets built; "
        },
        {
          "insert": "test/tool-schema-parity.test.ts",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true,
            "reference": {
              "kind": "source",
              "path": "packages/canvas-agent/test/tool-schema-parity.test.ts"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " pins the roster and the structural invariants every schema satisfies."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-roster-table-8": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-roster-table-8",
      "type": "structured-table",
      "props": {
        "title": "Thirty-two tools, in registration order",
        "columns": [
          "tool",
          "group",
          "the gesture"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "place_section",
            "Place",
            "draw a titled frame, which adopts whatever its edges already cover"
          ],
          [
            "place_sticky",
            "Place",
            "drop a note with its text already on it"
          ],
          [
            "place_shape",
            "Place",
            "the pick and the click — a shape or glyph at its default size, untitled"
          ],
          [
            "clone",
            "Place",
            "copy one object's kind, size, and look onto a new id"
          ],
          [
            "connect",
            "Place",
            "route an edge between two objects"
          ],
          [
            "move_to",
            "Arrange",
            "put a box's top-left corner at a point on the board"
          ],
          [
            "move_by",
            "Arrange",
            "nudge a box by an offset from where it already is"
          ],
          [
            "resize",
            "Arrange",
            "re-size a box to explicit dimensions, holding its top-left corner"
          ],
          [
            "match_size",
            "Arrange",
            "copy another box's width and height onto this one"
          ],
          [
            "align",
            "Arrange",
            "put a row or column of boxes on one shared edge or centerline"
          ],
          [
            "space_out",
            "Arrange",
            "re-pitch a run so the clear gap between neighbours is exactly what you ask for"
          ],
          [
            "update_text",
            "Content & appearance",
            "write the text of anything that carries text"
          ],
          [
            "change_color",
            "Content & appearance",
            "recolor anything that carries a color, edges included"
          ],
          [
            "change_shape",
            "Content & appearance",
            "swap what a shape is, and which way it points"
          ],
          [
            "fit_section",
            "Sections",
            "close a section around the children already inside it"
          ],
          [
            "change_section_border",
            "Sections",
            "restroke a frame's border"
          ],
          [
            "lock",
            "Sections",
            "protect a region — the frame alone, or the frame and everything in it"
          ],
          [
            "unlock",
            "Sections",
            "release a section's lock"
          ],
          [
            "style_edge",
            "Edges",
            "redraw an edge's line and arrowheads"
          ],
          [
            "change_connection",
            "Edges",
            "repoint one end of an edge; neither endpoint object changes"
          ],
          [
            "reroute",
            "Edges",
            "replace an edge's interior corners wholesale"
          ],
          [
            "shift_segment",
            "Edges",
            "slide one numbered segment of the route sideways"
          ],
          [
            "reset_route",
            "Edges",
            "hand an edge back to the auto-router"
          ],
          [
            "move_label",
            "Edges",
            "pin the label chip along the routed path"
          ],
          [
            "delete",
            "Delete",
            "remove one thing, with the cascade its kind implies"
          ],
          [
            "look",
            "Perceive, ask, finish",
            "study one framed region close up — rendered and measured"
          ],
          [
            "update_description",
            "Perceive, ask, finish",
            "replace the board's standing account wholesale"
          ],
          [
            "set_board_title",
            "Perceive, ask, finish",
            "rename the board"
          ],
          [
            "add_annotation",
            "Perceive, ask, finish",
            "anchor a question to one object as a thread the user answers later"
          ],
          [
            "reply_annotation",
            "Perceive, ask, finish",
            "post a reply into a thread without moving its status"
          ],
          [
            "resolve_request",
            "Perceive, ask, finish",
            "dispose one open request as done or declined, with a note"
          ],
          [
            "finalize",
            "Perceive, ask, finish",
            "end the run, with a proposal or without one"
          ]
        ]
      },
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-absorbed-heading-9": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-absorbed-heading-9",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Absorbed, not added"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-absorbed-lede-10": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-absorbed-lede-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Three calls a gesture surface might be expected to carry are not tools, because an existing tool already answers what they would ask. "
        },
        {
          "insert": "match_size",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is the counterexample and is a real gesture on the roster: peer sizing is its own motion, and it earns its own verb."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-absorbed-measure-11": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-absorbed-measure-11",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "measure",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " lives inside "
        },
        {
          "insert": "look",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "'s region readout. A framed region comes back rendered "
        },
        {
          "insert": "and",
          "attributes": {
            "italic": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " measured — per-pair gaps on each axis, row and column pitch, the section's free margins, ink share — so conformance is read rather than computed in context."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-absorbed-distribute-12": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-absorbed-distribute-12",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "distribute",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is subsumed by "
        },
        {
          "insert": "space_out",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". Equalizing inside a fixed span can never open a gap, and the agent always knows its target gap from the craft targets, so the gesture that sets the pitch covers both jobs."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-absorbed-route-13": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-absorbed-route-13",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "route_around",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " is not on the surface. Route cleanup is deliberate elbow work — "
        },
        {
          "insert": "shift_segment",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for one segment, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "reroute",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " for the whole path — not a hint handed to a solver."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-scope-heading-14": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-scope-heading-14",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "What the surface excludes"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-scope-lede-15": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-scope-lede-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Three capabilities sit outside the surface's scope. Each is buildable from what is on the roster, and each has a condition under which it is worth revisiting."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-scope-multi-16": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-scope-multi-16",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Multi-id variants",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " of "
        },
        {
          "insert": "move_to",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "move_by",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", "
        },
        {
          "insert": "change_color",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "delete",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — the UI's selection grammar. Batching would speed a run but cuts against one gesture, one operation; the two multi-id gestures that do exist, "
        },
        {
          "insert": "align",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "space_out",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", take a list because the arrangement itself is the gesture. Revisit once single-id traces show where batching earns its keep."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-scope-extend-17": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-scope-extend-17",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A quick-connect gesture",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " — an "
        },
        {
          "insert": "extend(fromId, id, direction, text?)",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " that drops a blank same-styled copy one half-width away, already wired, in one history entry. The surface builds the same result as a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "clone",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " followed by a "
        },
        {
          "insert": "connect",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-scope-annotation-18": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-scope-annotation-18",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Annotation-targeted creation and deletion.",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " "
        },
        {
          "insert": "add_annotation",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " anchors a thread to exactly one object — there are no intent or region targets — and "
        },
        {
          "insert": "delete",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " takes board ids only, never an annotation id. A thread is disposed with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "resolve_request",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ", not removed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-ts-ov-scope-close-19": {
      "id": "b-ts-ov-scope-close-19",
      "type": "constraint",
      "props": {
        "title": "The roster is the boundary"
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A capability the roster does not name is a capability the agent does not have. There is no escape hatch tool, no raw patch, and no free-form document write: the twenty-five gestures are the only way the draft changes."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
